  "raw": " life-saving drugs\n\nA carer admitted lying to police and her own boss after a palliative patient claimed she administered life-threatening medication equipment.\n\nMrs Hill tried to give Mrs Robson, of Elliot Close, Wilden, readings for use with her life support equipment one evening last year, defence lawyer Steve Brallier said. Mrs Robson was disputing whether she had been accepted by Warwickshire Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust or not at the time of her cardiac arrest on 24 August.\n\nWhen police arrived, nurse Julia Knight, 55, denied even being involved, laboratory tests confirmed and her employer who stresses that it does not hire anyone without them knowing proved after investigation she was responsible, he said.\n\nDespite hysterical accusations against the accused over 'accidental poisoning', she has never been taken off the standard psychiatric certificate allowing her continued work involving private patients.\n\nIt allowed her to return hours after the incident to administer horizontal ventilation (ventriculasp",
  "serialized": "life-saving drugs A carer admitted lying to police and her own boss after a palliative patient claimed she administered life-threatening medication equipment. Mrs Hill tried to give Mrs Robson, of Elliot Close, Wilden, readings for use with her life support equipment one evening last year, defence lawyer Steve Brallier said. Mrs Robson was disputing whether she had been accepted by Warwickshire Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust or not at the time of her cardiac arrest on 24 August. When police arrived, nurse Julia Knight, 55, denied even being involved, laboratory tests confirmed and her employer who stresses that it does not hire anyone without them knowing proved after investigation she was responsible, he said. Despite hysterical accusations against the accused over 'accidental poisoning', she has never been taken off the standard psychiatric certificate allowing her continued work involving private patients. It allowed her to return hours after the incident to administer horizontal ventilation (ventriculasp",
